Import linfit as L

Assuming the data points have uncertainty of 0.5 for y affects every data point for the weighing of the fit and the resulting fitted parameters. At 0.2, the data is closer to the fitted true line and therefore more precise because the uncertainty is reduced. If it was increased to 0.9, the parameter uncertainties increase and therefore data is further form the true line for the uncertainty is almost 1. Because every point is assigned the same uncertainty in this case for 0.5, the best-fit slope and intercept should change very little, while their uncertainties scale with the assumed value of sigma y. For lint, the fitted parameters are af (fitted intercept), bf (fitted slope). The other parameters in Linfit are a_unc and b_unc as their respective uncertainties, chisq (chi squared), prob (goodness of fit probability), covar (covariance matrix) and fit (fitted y values). 

